  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "When Anton demands to know why Viktor Petrovich is meddling in his kitchen, Barinov declares that since today is his daughter's wedding, he will inspect every single plate. Fed up with Barinov's antics, Anton storms out with his entire team.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему вы лезете на мою кухню?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Потому что это мой ресторан.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И сегодня свадьба моей дочери.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я буду контролировать каждое блюдо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ясно, тогда сами тут контролируйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Контролируйте дальше, уважаемый маэстро!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Проверяйте сами подачу каждого блюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Вы что тут вообще творите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Вы все с ума сошли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Здесь у вас настоящий цирк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добро пожаловать на эту кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ребята, быстро уходим за мной!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему вы лезете на мою кухню?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why are you meddling in my kitchen?' the guest raises the pitch on 'kitchen' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Потому что это мой ресторан.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Because this is my restaurant.' Notice how Russian expresses 'that is why' and 'restaurant' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И сегодня свадьба моей дочери.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And today is my daughter's wedding.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'of daughter'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я буду контролировать каждое блюдо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will supervise every dish.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'will be' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ясно, тогда сами тут контролируйте.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Clear enough, then supervise it here yourself.' the guest anchors the line on 'clear', while 'control' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Контролируйте дальше, уважаемый маэстро!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Keep supervising, respected maestro!' Notice how Russian expresses 'control' and 'maestro' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Проверяйте сами подачу каждого блюда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Check the plating of every dish yourself!' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'to check' before landing on 'of dish'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Вы что тут вообще творите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What on earth are you doing in here?' the guest brings out the contrast between 'you' and 'what' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Вы все с ума сошли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Have you all lost your minds?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'you' and finishing on 'went'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Здесь у вас настоящий цирк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have a real circus in here!' the guest brings out the contrast between 'here' and 'at' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добро пожаловать на эту кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Welcome to this kitchen.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'good' before landing on 'kitchen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ребята, быстро уходим за мной!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Guys, let us leave quickly, follow me!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'guys' and finishing on 'me'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
